# AsterOS host-side cross-compilation default config, auto-loaded by clang
# whenever it's invoked as "clang" from the directory this template is
# installed into (clang's own config-file mechanism: it looks for
# "<prog-name>.cfg" beside the executable -- see
# https://clang.llvm.org/docs/UsersManual.html#configuration-files).
# This is what makes `clang hello.m -o hello` produce a real AsterOS
# Mach-O without spelling out every flag by hand each time -- same recipe
# every previous phase's test/build.sh used explicitly (crt0.o +
# libc_start.o statically bring in _start, everything else resolved by
# AsterOS's own dyld at runtime against the real dylibs), just promoted to
# clang's own default-args mechanism instead of copy-pasted per test. Not
# a wrapper: this is still the real, unmodified clang driver/frontend/
# codegen and the real, unmodified host ld64 -- the config file only
# supplies default arguments, same as any real SDK's own defaults do.
#
# Template, not the real config: @ROOT@/@XCODE_CLANG_DIR@ get substituted
# by setup_host_cross_toolchain.sh into build/tools/asteros-sdk/bin/clang.cfg
# (build/ is always regenerated, never hand-edited -- this .in file is the
# tracked source of truth).
--target=x86_64-apple-macos10.15
-resource-dir=@XCODE_RESOURCE_DIR@
-fobjc-runtime=macosx
-nostdlibinc
-nostdlib
-isystem @ROOT@/userland/libc/include
-Wl,-no_pie
-Wl,-bind_at_load
-Wl,-e,_start
-Wl,-lto_library,@XCODE_LIBLTO@
@ROOT@/build/libc_obj/crt0.o
@ROOT@/build/libc_obj/libc_start.o
@ROOT@/build/libobjc_obj/libobjc.A.dylib
@ROOT@/build/libSystem_obj/libSystem.B.dylib
